@moduledoc """
OAuth2 client-credentials connections: how machines call the JSON:API.

An organization's owners and admins create a connection; the authorization
server behind `<%= inspect(@provider) %>` (selected by `OAUTH_PROVIDER`) holds the client and
issues access tokens for it. `<%= inspect(@web) %>.Plugs.LoadConnection` verifies those
tokens (`<%= inspect(@connections) %>.Tokens`) and turns a valid one into the Ash actor, a
`<%= inspect(@connection) %>`.

This domain keeps one row per client. The row, not the token, is what grants
access: revoking a connection deletes the client at the provider and marks the
row, and the plug only accepts tokens whose client has an unrevoked row, so a
token that is still within its lifetime stops working on the next request.
"""

use Ash.Domain, otp_app: <%= inspect(@app) %>, extensions: [AshPaperTrail.Domain]

paper_trail do
  include_versions? true
end

resources do
  resource <%= inspect(@connection) %>
end

@doc "The active connection registered under `client_id`; `{:ok, nil}` when there is none."
@spec active_by_client_id(String.t() | nil) ::
        {:ok, <%= inspect(@connection) %>.t() | nil} | {:error, term()}
def active_by_client_id(nil), do: {:ok, nil}

def active_by_client_id(client_id) do
  <%= inspect(@connection) %>
  |> Ash.Query.for_read(:by_client_id, %{client_id: client_id})
  |> Ash.read_one(authorize?: false)
end

@doc "The audience access tokens must carry (`OAUTH_AUDIENCE`); clients send it as `audience=` when they ask for a token."
@spec audience() :: String.t()
def audience, do: <%= inspect(@provider) %>.config()[:audience]
